course: dictionary
lesson: 14798
title: On time, every time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Punctually» is an adverb. It tells you how or when something happens. When something happens punctually, it happens at exactly the right time, not late. Look at the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «The train left punctually at nine.» The clue is "at nine": the train left at the right time, with no delay. Now try the meaning in the sentence: "The train left at exactly the right time, not late, at nine." It still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The word also means doing something regularly on time, every time. «She pays her bills punctually.» This tells you she never forgets and never pays late. In school, arriving and handing in work punctually is a good habit. In a maths word problem, punctually means there is no delay, so use the exact time you are given.
fact: Punctually means at exactly the right time, not late.
fact: «Punctually» can also mean regularly on time, every time.
fact: «The train left punctually at nine.» The train left at nine, with no delay.
fact: «She pays her bills punctually.» She always pays on time.
fact: In a maths word problem, punctually means there is no delay, so the time is exact.
exercise: «The bus left punctually at eight o'clock.» What does punctually mean here? | Slowly and carefully | Much later than planned | *At exactly the right time, not late | Very fast with lots of noise
exercise: «She pays her bills punctually.» What does punctually mean here? | Only just, at the last second | Very quietly | *Regularly on time, every time | Sometimes, when she feels like it
exercise: Find and copy the word that means at exactly the right time. | slowly | *punctually | barely | yesterday
test: «The train arrived punctually, so Sam was not late for school.» Why was Sam not late? | Sam ran all the way to school | *The train arrived at the right time | The train was very fast | The train was cancelled
test: Mrs Lee says, «Please start punctually.» What does she want? | Start very slowly | *Start at exactly the right time | Start after everyone has gone home | Start with a loud noise
exam: «The concert started punctually at seven, so the children were in their seats.» What does punctually tell us? | *The concert started at exactly seven, with no delay | The concert went on for hours | The concert was in a different place | The concert was late
